  "id": "RAW_9d4ca39497",
  "title": "因果模型需要因果数据——Xaira 的 X-Cell 模型用于药物发现（Bo Wang 与 Ci Chu，首席发现官兼首席 AI 科学家）",
  "url": "https://www.latent.space/p/xaira",
  "date": "2026-07-22 03:34:06",
  "author": "RJ Honicky",
  "siteName": "Latent.Space",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <div dir=\"auto\" class=\"body markup\">\n   <h1 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Bet on information\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h1>\n   <p><span>If </span><em>test loss flatlines</em><span> after 1.5B parameters while </span><em>training loss continues to drop</em><span> as you scale, that tells you that your model is </span><em>limited by the amount of information</em><span> in your data.</span></p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_e6c52f8c-8d38-4f63-8daa-ff6ab52e3aa5_827x883.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\">\n          <svg role=\"img\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n           <g>\n            <title></title><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path>\n           </g>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p></p>\n   <p><span>Training on a single, smallish data set exposed an information gap: the 3.1B model falls off the scaling trend. Neither parameters nor compute will improve performance past this wall. For predicting changes to gene expression, you need more </span><em>information rich data</em><span>.</span></p>\n   <p>This is what Chu and Bo’s teams have done, and here is what ~30x the information buys you:</p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20260721194514_034901bc-82c1-4711-8be6-547c1db9cfef_491x856.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\">\n          <svg role=\"img\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n           <g>\n            <title></title><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path>\n           </g>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p></p>\n   <p>Now we can scale with parameters and training compute! We don’t know how much this effort costed, but we can guess that data collection experiments and infrastructure was a few tens of millions, and compute + headcount + research was a few million. The budget looks like a RL rollout budget, rather than a data rich pre-training one.</p>\n   <p><span>We were lucky enough to have the two central figures in this story on our podcast. Taking the lead from Ci Chu and Bo Wang, Xaira Therapeutics is betting that </span><em>information rich</em><span> data is the key to AI-driven drug development. Chu </span><a href=\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260706699581/en/Xaira-Therapeutics-Announces-the-Appointment-of-Dr.-Ian-McCaffery-as-SVP-Translational-Science-and-Early-Clinical-Development-and-the-Promotions-of-Dr.-Ci-Chu-to-Chief-Discovery-Officer-and-Dr.-Bo-Wang-to-Chief-AI-Scientist\">was recently promoted</a><span> to Chief Discovery Officer and Bo to Chief AI Scientist</span><span style=\"min-width:0;\"><a id=\"footnote-anchor-1\" href=\"#footnote-1\" target=\"_self\" class=\"footnote-anchor\">1</a></span><span>, underscoring just how strategic Xaira considers this bet.</span></p>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Reverse engineering the human cell\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p>If you had to figure out how a human cell works, what would you do? A good place to start might be by documenting what genes are expressed (e.g. what RNA is floating around) in different kinds of cells, in different circumstances.</p>\n   <p><span>That is </span><a href=\"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/\">CELLxGENE</a><span>, a database of 168M cells built by Chan Zuckerberg Institute that maps each cell to a count of how many times 20K-30K genes were detected in that cell, plus detailed metadata about </span><em>every cell</em><span>. A ~4 trillion-entry matrix.</span></p>\n   <p><span>If the Protein Data Bank (PDB) unlocked structural biology models [link Boltz, BioHub], CellXGene has done the same thing for Virtual Cell models. Like PDB, CELLxGENE has inspired a zoo of AI models of RNA expression; so much so that RNA expression models have become synonymous with Virtual Cell models. Bo Wang built one of the most influential, </span><a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-024-02201-0\">scGPT</a><span>, that became the starting point for Xaira’s new model.</span></p>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">RNA expression ≠ Virtual Cell\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p><span>Models trained on CELLxGENE </span><em>describe</em><span> the relationship between cell types and cell states, but they are not good at </span><em>predicting</em><span> what will happen if we make changes to RNA expression. Changes in gene expression are </span><em>highly</em><span> correlated, and its is difficult (impossible) to figure out what causes what in most cases.</span></p>\n   <p><span>If you could “turn the dial down” on one gene at a time, however, then you would be able to observe what is upstream and downstream of a given gene</span><span style=\"min-width:0;\"><a id=\"footnote-anchor-2\" href=\"#footnote-2\" target=\"_self\" class=\"footnote-anchor\">2</a></span><span>. You could tell if A → B &amp; C or B → A &amp; C or B → A, C → B → … If you did this for all of the genes, then maybe you could train a model that could predict what would happen to a cell if you change a gene (e.g. with a drug or a gene edit). Or maybe you could figure out the least invasive way to change a particular gene’s expression.</span></p>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">X-Atlas → X-Cell\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p>This is exactly what Chu and Bo’s teams have done. The data set is called X-Atlas and the model is called X-Cell.</p>\n   <p>In this episode, we discuss:</p>\n   <ul>\n    <li>\n     <p>Why the team abandoned autoregression for diffusion</p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n     <p>The CRISPR-based experiments that run millions of tests in parallel, and generate the raw data for X-Atlas and X-cell</p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n     <p>Generalization to real lab experiments in real human cells</p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n     <p>Beating the linear baseline that has outperformed previous models</p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n     <p>Justifying a kitchen-sink of priors, and how that stacks up vs. data and architecture</p>\n    </li>\n   </ul>\n   <p>Bo also shared with us some of the (major) advantages he has as an academic vs. industry leader, and how his labs keep up with the breakneck pace of AI innovation.</p>\n   <div id=\"media-c6b8f2cc-bb4d-4b75-baad-1b9f588a60af\" class=\"videoScrollTarget-SzB20Y\"></div>\n   <p>Check out the full episode on YouTube, or your favorite podcasting platform!</p>\n   <div id=\"youtube2-2AdS-2uuH80\" class=\"youtube-wrap\">\n    <div class=\"youtube-inner\">\n     <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/2AdS-2uuH80?rel=0&amp;autoplay=0&amp;showinfo=0&amp;enablejsapi=0\" frameborder=\"0\" loading=\"lazy\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" width=\"728\" height=\"409\"></iframe>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"footnote\">\n    <a id=\"footnote-1\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-1\" target=\"_self\" class=\"footnote-number\">1</a>\n    <div class=\"footnote-content\">\n     <p>These promotions happened after we recorded the episode</p>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"footnote\">\n    <a id=\"footnote-2\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-2\" target=\"_self\" class=\"footnote-number\">2</a>\n    <div class=\"footnote-content\">\n     <p>There can be cycles in the chain reaction, of course, and there can be second, third, etc. order effects (meaning things that only happen when multiple genes change at once), but the first order effects are a great place to start, and might tell us a lot of what we need to know.</p>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "Xaira Therapeutics 通过 CRISPR 生成扰动数据，构建用于药物发现的因果模型（X-Cell），克服了观察性 RNA 表达数据的信息极限。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "Xaira Therapeutics 通过 CRISPR 生成扰动数据，构建用于药物发现的因果模型（X-Cell），克服了观察性 RNA 表达数据的信息极限。",
  "summary": "本文涵盖了与 Xaira 首席发现官 Ci Chu 和首席 AI 科学家 Bo Wang 的对话，讨论他们构建用于药物发现的因果 AI 模型的方法。文章解释了在大型观察性数据集（如 CELLxGENE）上训练的传统 RNA 表达模型虽然能很好地描述相关性，但无法预测遗传扰动的影响，因为它们缺乏因果信息。为了解决这个问题，Xaira 生成了 X-Atlas，这是一个基于 CRISPR 的单基因扰动实验的大规模数据集，每个细胞提供约 30 倍的信息。这使得他们能够训练 X-Cell，一个基于扩散的模型，可以预测基因表达如何响应扰动而变化，并推广到真实实验室实验，且优于此前占主导地位的线性基线。文章还讨论了扩展洞见、选择扩散而非自回归的原因，以及这一赌注对 Xaira 的战略重要性。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "观察性 RNA 表达数据在扩展模型参数时达到信息极限。",
      "explanation": "当参数达到 15 亿后，测试损失趋于平稳，而训练损失仍在下降，这表明模型受限于数据信息而非容量。"
    },
    {
      "point": "来自 CRISPR 扰动的因果数据释放了预测能力。",
      "explanation": "X-Atlas 通过测量单基因扰动的影响，每个细胞提供 30 倍的信息，使模型能够学习因果关系而非相关性。"
    },
    {
      "point": "X-Cell 使用扩散而非自回归，以更好地建模扰动。",
      "explanation": "在该领域，扩散比自回归方法更好地处理基因表达变化的噪声和高维依赖关系。"
    },
    {
      "point": "该模型可泛化到真实实验室实验，并击败了线性基线。",
      "explanation": "X-Cell 准确预测了真实人类细胞实验的结果，超越了此前优于其他深度学习方法的简单线性模型。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "如果参数达到 15 亿后测试损失趋于平稳，而随着规模扩大训练损失持续下降，那就说明你的模型受限于数据中的信息量。",
    "在 CELLxGENE 上训练的模型描述了细胞类型与细胞状态之间的关系，但它们不擅长预测如果我们改变 RNA 表达会发生什么。"
  ],
